# Tool registry, internal tools API and the `graph-manager-mcp` command

## What to build

The server side backbone of "agent tools" in graph-manager (`apps/graph-manager`). Agents opened in graph-manager terminals will get tools through one MCP server, `graph-manager-mcp`: a dependency-free stdio command on the terminals' `PATH` that lists and calls tools through graph-manager's internal API. This slice delivers:

1. A tool registry for graph-execution developers: `src/server/tools/types.ts` (the `GmTool` interface) and `src/server/tools/index.ts` (`TOOLS`, `toolList()`), plus a way for tests to inject tools (`BuildAppOptions.tools`).
2. Two internal routes, authenticated like `/api/internal/sandbox-runs`: `GET /api/internal/tools` and `POST /api/internal/tools/:name`.
3. A per-terminal env var `GM_TERMINAL_ID=<terminal id>` so the MCP process knows which terminal called it.
4. The MCP command `src/server/mcp.ts` (built to `dist/server/mcp.js`) and a `<binDir>/graph-manager-mcp` launcher script written at startup.

`TOOLS` ships **empty** in this slice (a later slice adds `open_start_run`); tests use an injected test tool. Read the spec `docs/prd/agent-tools.md` (sections "Tool registry", "Internal API", "MCP command", "Terminals") — it is the contract.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `docs/prd/agent-tools.md` — the spec; the Requirements sections named above.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts` (lines 33–57: `AppContext`, `BuildAppOptions`; lines 68–86: `binDir`, `internal` token, `writeGraphExecutionShim`, `TerminalManager` with `extraEnv`; lines 128–141: route registration) — where the context, options and routes are wired.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/internal.ts` (whole file, 122 lines) — the existing internal route: token check `tokenMatches` (lines 55–62), loopback check `LOOPBACK` (line 21 and line 77), `workspaceOf` (lines 64–71). Mirror and reuse these.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/internal.test.ts` (lines 1–60) — how internal routes are tested: `buildApp(config, { store, webDir, viewCache: false, internalToken: TOKEN })`, `app.inject` with `authorization: Bearer ${TOKEN}`, a workspace created under `config.workspacesDir/github/octo/hello` with `git init`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/terminals.ts` (lines 22–31 `CreateTerminal`; 47–52 `extraEnv`; 83 `STRIPPED_ENV`; 113–127 `terminalEnv`; 129–143 `writeGraphExecutionShim`; 163–190 `create`/`spawn`) — where `GM_TERMINAL_ID` goes and the shim-writing pattern to mirror.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/terminals.test.ts` (lines 1–33 helpers `setup`/`run`; the test "sets the handoff env and strips GM_PASSWORD" near line 68) — pattern for env tests.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/shim.ts` (whole file) — the dependency-free style (`node:` imports only), `main()` guarded by `process.argv[1] === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)`, and how it reaches `GM_INTERNAL_URL` with `GM_INTERNAL_TOKEN`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/shim.dist.test.ts` — pattern for a test of a built file under `dist/server/`, skipped until it is built.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/server/workspaces.ts` (lines 6–20 `Workspace`; `listWorkspaces` line 33) — the workspace type.

## Patterns to follow

**Registry types** (`src/server/tools/types.ts`):
```ts
import type { z } from "zod";
import type { AppContext } from "../app.js";
import type { TerminalInfo } from "../terminals.js";
import type { Workspace } from "../workspaces.js";

export interface ToolContext {
  ctx: AppContext;
  /** The calling terminal. */
  terminal: TerminalInfo;
  /** The terminal's workspace (from terminal.workspaceId, else the workspace containing cwd), if any. */
  workspace?: Workspace;
  /** The MCP process's cwd, absolute. */
  cwd: string;
}
export interface ToolResult { text: string; isError?: boolean }
export interface GmTool<S extends z.ZodType = z.ZodType> {
  /** snake_case, unique. */
  name: string;
  description: string;
  input: S;
  run(input: z.infer<S>, tc: ToolContext): Promise<ToolResult>;
}
/** Keeps the input type when registering: `defineTool({ ... })`. */
export function defineTool<S extends z.ZodType>(t: GmTool<S>): GmTool<S> { return t; }
```

**Registry** (`src/server/tools/index.ts`):
```ts
import { z } from "zod";
import type { GmTool } from "./types.js";
/** graph-manager's tools for agents in its terminals. Add a tool: write src/server/tools/<name>.ts and list it here. */
export const TOOLS: GmTool[] = [];
export function toolList(tools: GmTool[] = TOOLS) {
  return tools.map((t) => ({ name: t.name, description: t.description, inputSchema: z.toJSONSchema(t.input) }));
}
```
zod is v4 (`apps/graph-manager/package.json`: `"zod": "^4.6.7"`), which has `z.toJSONSchema`. If `GmTool<S>` vs `GmTool` variance gives type errors in the array, type the array as `GmTool<any>[]` with an eslint-disable comment, or store `GmTool<z.ZodType>`.

**AppContext / options** — add optional fields, as the comment on `AppContext` says ("Later features may add optional fields"):
```ts
// AppContext
/** Tools for agents in terminals (src/server/tools). */
tools: GmTool[];
// BuildAppOptions
/** Replaces the registry's tools (tests). */
tools?: GmTool[];
// in buildApp
const ctx: AppContext = { config, store, terminals, viewCache, sandboxes, internal, tools: opts.tools ?? TOOLS };
```

**Internal auth** — factor the token + loopback checks from the existing `POST /api/internal/sandbox-runs` handler (internal.ts lines 74–77) into one helper used by all three routes, e.g.
```ts
/** 401/403 for a request that is not a terminal of this server; undefined when it may pass. */
function denied(req: FastifyRequest, ctx: AppContext): { code: number; error: string } | undefined
```
and keep the sandbox route's behaviour and messages (`bad internal token`, `only from this machine`) unchanged.

**Errors** — zod `parse` errors already become 400 `{ error: "<path>: <message>" }` via the app error handler (app.ts lines 89–95). For tool input validation use `safeParse` and return a 200 tool result instead (spec).

**Terminal env** — `GM_TERMINAL_ID` is set per terminal in `TerminalManager.spawn` (it has the term id: change `spawn(argv, cwd, cols, rows)` to also take the id, or build env in `create`/`restart`). Add `"GM_TERMINAL_ID"` to `STRIPPED_ENV` (line 83) so an outer graph-manager's value is dropped from the base env.

**Launcher script** — mirror `writeGraphExecutionShim` (terminals.ts 129–143):
```ts
/** Writes `<binDir>/graph-manager-mcp` running `mcpJs` with node; false on Windows or when mcpJs is missing. */
export function writeMcpShim(binDir: string, mcpJs: string): boolean {
  if (process.platform === "win32" || !existsSync(mcpJs)) return false;
  mkdirSync(binDir, { recursive: true });
  const file = path.join(binDir, "graph-manager-mcp");
  writeFileSync(file, `#!/bin/sh\nexec node ${JSON.stringify(mcpJs)} "$@"\n`, { mode: 0o755 });
  chmodSync(file, 0o755);
  return true;
}
```
GOTCHA: in `app.ts` today `binDir` is passed to `TerminalManager` only when the graph-execution shim was written (`hasShim`); in tests `graphExecutionBin` is `"graph-execution"` (not an absolute .js), so `hasShim` is false. Pass `binDir` when **either** shim was written: `const hasMcp = writeMcpShim(binDir, fileURLToPath(new URL("./mcp.js", import.meta.url)));` and `binDir: hasShim || hasMcp ? binDir : undefined`. When running under vitest from `src/`, `./mcp.js` resolves to `src/server/mcp.js`, which does not exist (only `mcp.ts`), so `hasMcp` is false in tests — that is fine.

## Step-by-step tasks

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/tools/types.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: `ToolContext`, `ToolResult`, `GmTool`, `defineTool` as above.

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/tools/index.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: `TOOLS` (empty for now, with the "add a tool" comment) and `toolList(tools)`.
- **GOTCHA**: a later slice appends `openStartRun` to `TOOLS`; keep it a plain array literal.

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/tools/index.test.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: for every entry of `TOOLS` (the test must pass with an empty array and keep working when tools are added): name matches `/^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$/` and is unique, description is non-empty, `toolList()` entry's `inputSchema.type === "object"`. Also a test with a local test tool (`z.object({ a: z.string() })`) checking `toolList([tool])[0].inputSchema.required` equals `["a"]`.

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/app.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: `tools` on `AppContext` and `BuildAppOptions`; `writeMcpShim`; binDir rule above.
- **IMPORTS**: `import { TOOLS } from "./tools/index.js"; import type { GmTool } from "./tools/types.js";`, `writeMcpShim` from `./terminals.js`.

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/terminals.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: `GM_TERMINAL_ID` in each spawned terminal's env (also after `restart`, same id), `STRIPPED_ENV` entry, `writeMcpShim`.
- **VALIDATE**: new test in `terminals.test.ts`: `run(mgr, dir, ["/bin/sh", "-c", "echo id=$GM_TERMINAL_ID"])` prints `id=t1`; and a base env with `GM_TERMINAL_ID: "outer"` still prints the terminal's own id. A test for `writeMcpShim` (skipped on win32): writes an executable file containing `exec node` and the path; returns false for a missing file.

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/internal.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**:
  - `GET /api/internal/tools` → `200 { tools: toolList(ctx.tools) }`.
  - `POST /api/internal/tools/:name`, body `z.object({ terminalId: z.string().min(1), cwd: z.string().min(1), input: z.unknown().optional() })`:
    - tool not in `ctx.tools` → 404 `{ error: "unknown tool <name>" }`;
    - `ctx.terminals.get(terminalId)` undefined → 400 `{ error: "unknown terminal <id>" }`;
    - `cwd` not absolute → 400 `{ error: "cwd must be an absolute path" }`;
    - workspace: `terminal.workspaceId` → `resolveWorkspace(path.resolve(ctx.config.workspacesDir), id)`, else `workspaceOf(ctx.config.workspacesDir, cwd)`;
    - `tool.input.safeParse(input ?? {})` failing → 200 `{ text: "invalid arguments: " + z.prettifyError(err) (or the first issue's path + message), isError: true }`;
    - otherwise 200 `await tool.run(data, { ctx, terminal, workspace, cwd })`. A thrown error → 200 `{ text: <message>, isError: true }` (log it with `req.log.error`).
  - Both routes use the shared token + loopback check.
- **IMPORTS**: `toolList` from `../tools/index.js`, `resolveWorkspace` from `../workspaces.js`.

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/routes/internal-tools.test.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: build the app with `internalToken: "t0ken"` and `tools: [echoTool]` where `echoTool = defineTool({ name: "echo_ws", description: "test", input: z.object({ say: z.string() }), run: async (i, tc) => ({ text: `${i.say}:${tc.workspace?.id ?? "none"}:${tc.terminal.id}` }) })`. Create a workspace dir `ws/github/octo/hello` with `.git` (see routes/terminals.test.ts line 20: `mkdir(path.join(config.workspacesDir, "github", "o", "r", ".git"), { recursive: true })`). Create a terminal with `ctx`-less API: `POST /api/terminals` with the session cookie (login as in `test-helpers.ts` `appWithLogin`, or `app.inject` login) and `{ workspaceId: "github~octo~hello" }`, then:
  - `GET /api/internal/tools` without token → 401; with token → lists `echo_ws` with `inputSchema.required` `["say"]`.
  - `POST /api/internal/tools/echo_ws` `{ terminalId, cwd: <ws path>, input: { say: "hi" } }` → 200 `{ text: "hi:github~octo~hello:t1" }`.
  - invalid input `{ say: 1 }` → 200 with `isError: true` and text starting `invalid arguments`.
  - unknown tool → 404 `unknown tool nope`; unknown terminal → 400 `unknown terminal t99`.
  - skip on win32 like the terminal route tests (`describe.skipIf(process.platform === "win32")`), since it spawns a PTY.

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/mcp.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT** (only `node:` imports; no zod, no app imports — it must start fast from `dist/server` alone, like `shim.ts`):
  ```ts
  export type Json = Record<string, unknown>;
  export interface McpEnv { GM_INTERNAL_URL?: string; GM_INTERNAL_TOKEN?: string; GM_TERMINAL_ID?: string }
  /** One JSON-RPC message in, the response out (undefined for notifications). */
  export async function handleMessage(msg: Json, env: McpEnv, cwd: string, fetchFn: typeof fetch): Promise<Json | undefined>
  ```
  - `initialize` → `{ jsonrpc: "2.0", id, result: { protocolVersion: params.protocolVersion ?? "2025-06-18", capabilities: { tools: {} }, serverInfo: { name: "graph-manager", version: "0.1.0" } } }`.
  - any message without `id` (notifications such as `notifications/initialized`) → undefined.
  - `ping` → `result: {}`.
  - `tools/list` → `GET ${url}/api/internal/tools` with `authorization: Bearer <token>`; `result: { tools }` (each `{ name, description, inputSchema }`). Without the three env vars, or on a network/HTTP error, `result: { tools: [] }` (log the reason to stderr).
  - `tools/call` → `POST ${url}/api/internal/tools/${encodeURIComponent(params.name)}` body `{ terminalId, cwd, input: params.arguments ?? {} }`; `result: { content: [{ type: "text", text }], isError }`. Without env: `isError: true`, text `graph-manager tools work only in a graph-manager terminal`. HTTP error: `isError: true`, text = the body's `error` or `graph-manager answered <status>`. Network error: `isError: true`, `graph-manager did not answer at <url>: <message>`.
  - unknown method → `error: { code: -32601, message: "method not found: <method>" }`.
  - `main()`: read stdin with `node:readline` line by line, `JSON.parse` each non-empty line (parse error → respond `error: { code: -32700, message: "parse error" }`, `id: null`), write `JSON.stringify(response) + "\n"` to stdout. Responses may complete out of order; that is allowed in JSON-RPC. Exit when stdin ends (after pending responses are written).
  - Guard: `if (process.argv[1] && path.resolve(process.argv[1]) === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) void main();` (copy from shim.ts last line).

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/mcp.test.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: unit tests of `handleMessage` with a fake `fetch` (`vi.fn(async () => new Response(JSON.stringify({ tools: [...] }), { status: 200 }))`): initialize echoes the protocol version; notification → undefined; tools/list forwards the bearer token and URL; tools/list without env → `[]` and fetch not called; tools/call body contains `terminalId`, `cwd`, `input`; HTTP 404 → `isError` with the server's error; fetch throwing → `isError` with `did not answer`; unknown method → -32601.

### CREATE `apps/graph-manager/src/server/mcp.dist.test.ts`
- **IMPLEMENT**: skipped unless `dist/server/mcp.js` exists (pattern: shim.dist.test.ts). Start `buildApp` with `tools: [echoTool]`, `internalToken`, `app.listen({ port: 0, host: "127.0.0.1" })`, create a terminal (as above) to get a terminal id, then spawn `node dist/server/mcp.js` (`node:child_process` `spawn`, env `{ ...process.env, GM_INTERNAL_URL: "http://127.0.0.1:<port>", GM_INTERNAL_TOKEN, GM_TERMINAL_ID }`), write `initialize` and `tools/list` lines, and read the responses: `tools/list` contains `echo_ws`. A second case with no GM_* env: `tools/list` returns `[]`. Kill the child at the end.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `GET /api/internal/tools` → 401 without the token, 200 `{ tools: [{ name, description, inputSchema }] }` with it.
- [ ] `POST /api/internal/tools/:name` behaves as specified for success, invalid input (200, `isError: true`), unknown tool (404) and unknown terminal (400).
- [ ] The existing `/api/internal/sandbox-runs` tests still pass unchanged.
- [ ] Every terminal has `GM_TERMINAL_ID` equal to its own id, also after restart; an inherited value is replaced.
- [ ] `npm run build -w graph-manager` produces `apps/graph-manager/dist/server/mcp.js`; started from `dist/` the server writes `<dataDir>/bin/graph-manager-mcp`, and terminals have that dir on `PATH`.
- [ ] `mcp.ts` imports only `node:` modules.
- [ ] Tests pass: `npm test -w graph-manager`.

## Validation commands

```bash
npm run build -w graph-execution && npm run build -w graph-manager
npm run typecheck && npm run lint
npm test -w graph-manager -- src/server/mcp src/server/tools src/server/routes/internal src/server/terminals
npm test -w graph-manager
```
